{"ts":"2026-08-28T13:17:05.003Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"7405dc9b453c8154184ac8fe","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"ops-jhc8"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The publish-attestation scan judged shell text with a regular expression, so real unattested publishes scanned clean"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The guard decided whether any publish omits provenance by blanking quoted spans and splitting the remainder on three operators. Blanking deletes the very argument under audit, so a publish carrying an attestation reads as one without it, and the reverse is worse: an eval or a bash dash-c wrapping a publish disappears from the scan entirely, leaving an attested sibling elsewhere in the file to carry the audit to green. The operator split also misses a backgrounding ampersand, a pipe written without surrounding spaces, and command substitution. Replaced by a real tokeniser that resolves what each command actually runs."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:release","area:supply-chain","type:defect"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-28T13:17:05.003Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-28T13:17:05.003Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"658811e30dba57be77f837c61837cbf20297fc9e69d27fb98e5e177e26f2063c","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"ts":"2026-08-28T13:17:14.415Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"7405dc9b453c8154184ac8fe","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-28T13:17:14.415Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-28T13:17:14.415Z","author":"claude","text":"Extracted scripts/shell-command-scan.ts: a tokeniser that tracks single, double and backslash quoting per character while keeping the quoted text in the token, splits on the full operator set (semicolon, ampersand, double-ampersand, pipe, double-pipe, newline) regardless of surrounding whitespace, and unwraps interpreter shells so that eval and bash dash-c bodies are re-scanned as commands rather than swallowed as string arguments. The attestation guard now asks the tokeniser for command name and arguments instead of pattern-matching text. Covered to 100/100/100/100; test/coverage-gate.test.ts stub updated to enumerate the new source file, which the gate requires."}]}],"before_hash":"658811e30dba57be77f837c61837cbf20297fc9e69d27fb98e5e177e26f2063c","after_hash":"0464d4e5f8000a99dc8e0c82f150d9a41ab89cc802cf6b2e445b157961baba3d","item_hash_version":2,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
